+# SPEC: JSONL custom-agent text folding (#184)
+
+Status: draft
+Owner: dmuxai
+Created: 2026-11-07
+Baseline: `origin/main`
+Related: GitHub #184, SPEC-custom-agent-provider (FR-2442), SPEC-grok-runner (FR-916)
+
+## 1. Decision summary
+
+Custom JSONL agents used to glue every text chunk into the final reply with no separator, and could report `ok: true` after several tool calls when only interim status text arrived. DmuxAI adds an optional `text_mode` (`last` | `concat`) on `[[agents.custom]]` JSONL runners. The default is `last`, keeping only the text block after the last `tool_when` / `text_break_when` boundary. `concat` preserves every part and inserts a newline between segments when no paragraph break is pending. The built-in opencode preset stays on `concat` so narration plus a final answer still stream together. When at least two tools ran and `last` dropped earlier blocks, a short leftover reply fails as `interim_unfinished`.
+
+## 2. Scope
+
+### In scope
+
+- `text_mode` config, default `last`, `ReplyCollector` folding, concat newlines.
+- `interim_unfinished` when multi-tool interim narration remains under 200 characters.
+- Opencode preset `text_mode = concat` and `text_break_when` for `tool_use`.
+- Docs in `docs/agents/custom-agents.md`.
+
+### Out of scope / non-goals
+
+- Heuristic detection of “final report” wording.
+- Changing non-JSONL (`output = "text"`) agents.
+- Runner fallback on `interim_unfinished`.
+
+## 4. Requirements
+
+| ID | Priority | Preconditions / trigger | Required observable result | Failure or boundary behavior | Evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| FR-2450 | Must | JSONL custom agent; `text_mode` unset or `last`. | Only text after the last `tool_when` or `text_break_when` line is stored and emitted as the final reply. | `output = text` ignores `text_mode`. | TC-2451 |
+| FR-2451 | Must | JSONL custom agent with `text_mode = "concat"`. | Every matching text part is kept; consecutive parts without a pending paragraph break join with a single newline. | Paragraph breaks (`text_break_when`) still use `\n\n` via existing logic. | TC-2450, TC-2442 |
+| FR-2452 | Must | JSONL agent with `tool_when`, default `text_mode = last`, at least two tool invocations, two or more prior text blocks dropped, non-empty reply under 200 chars. | Turn fails with `error_kind` `interim_unfinished` and a message naming retry or `text_mode = concat`. Headless `ok: false`. | Long final replies or a single-tool turn still succeed. | TC-2454, TC-2452 |
+| FR-2453 | Must | Built-in opencode preset. | `text_mode = concat` and `text_break_when` on `tool_use` so narration and final answers match FR-2440 behavior. | — | TC-2453, TC-2440 |
+
+## 5. Acceptance scenarios and test design
+
+| Test ID | Requirement IDs | Type | Setup / Given | Action / When | Oracle / Then | Automated location |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| TC-2450 | FR-2451 | unit | concat spec, two text lines | collect | reply joined with `\n` | `tc_2450_concat_mode_joins_text_parts_with_newlines` |
+| TC-2451 | FR-2450 | unit | last spec, tool between texts | collect | only text after tool | `tc_2451_last_mode_keeps_final_text_block_after_tools` |
+| TC-2452 | FR-2452 | integration | fake `jsonl_interim` script | run turn | `interim_unfinished` | `tc_2452_interim_narration_only_fails_with_interim_unfinished` |
+| TC-2453 | FR-2453 | unit | opencode preset | inspect | `concat` text_mode | `tc_2453_opencode_preset_uses_concat_text_mode` |
+| TC-2454 | FR-2452 | unit | multi-tool JSONL lines | collect + `interim_unfinished()` | true | `tc_2454_interim_unfinished_after_multi_tool_status_only` |
+
+## 8. Review and test exit criteria
+
+- `cargo test tc_2450 tc_2451 tc_2452 tc_2453 tc_2454`
+- `python3 scripts/check-spec.py --all` and `python3 scripts/check-tc-links.py`
